> Explain why deterministic validation matters when optimizing a GPU inference kernel.
# Why Deterministic Validation Matters for GPU Inference Kernels

When optimizing GPU kernels, determinism in validation isn't just a nice-to-have—it's foundational to trusting your optimizations. Here's why it matters:

## 1. Isolating Correctness from Optimizations

GPU optimizations introduce many sources of nondeterminism:
- **Floating-point reordering** — parallel reductions sum elements in different orders, producing slightly different results
- **Non-deterministic kernel launch order** — when multiple kernels write to the same memory
- **Atomic operation ordering** — concurrent updates don't have a guaranteed order

